    "q-73612": {
      "dom_id": "step-q73612",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 2 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd and $5$th columns:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 2 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot columns are the $2$nd and $4$th columns.",
