    "q-130957": {
      "dom_id": "step-q130957",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $B,$ given by\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we need to convert $B$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $3$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $3.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
