    "q-73630": {
      "dom_id": "step-q73630",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $C,$ given by\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we need to convert $C$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $C$ has $4$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $4.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
