    "q-73635": {
      "dom_id": "step-q73635",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $Q,$ given by\n\n$$\nQ=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we need to convert $Q$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $Q$ has $4$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $4.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
