    "q-35459": {
      "dom_id": "step-q35459",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $D,$ given by\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -8 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we need to convert $D$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -8 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(\\frac{2}{7}){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $D$ has $5$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $5.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
