    "q-35757": {
      "dom_id": "step-q35757",
      "name": "Question 16",
      "problem": "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]?\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th columns.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-35757-a",
