    "q-131307": {
      "dom_id": "step-q131307",
      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $P,$ given by\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 2 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 9 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -6 & -3\\end{aligned}]?\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we need to convert $P$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 2 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 9 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -6 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 2 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 9 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -6 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+2{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 2 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 9 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $P$ has $4$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $2$nd, $3$rd, $5$th, and $6$th columns.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
